---
/*
 * Step 1 — sign in.
 *
 * THE BUTTON IS A STUB AND IT SAYS SO OUT LOUD. Nothing on this page is wired to the server,
 * so the only honest outcome of pressing "Continue with GitHub" is "this is not connected
 * yet". That is what it reports — after a real idle → busy → resolved transition, because the
 * transition is the part worth building. It never renders a signed-in identity, never shows a
 * handle or an avatar, and never implies an account now exists.
 *
 * WHAT CHANGED, AND WHY THE OLD WORDING IS DEAD. The panel used to say "coswarm has no
 * self-serve signup on the server" (that was the product's name at the time — it is
 * CommonSwarm now). That is now FALSE and is kept here only so it is not
 * re-derived: `create_workspace` is handled by createSelfServeWorkspace() in
 * supabase/functions/command/index.ts. Two things are true instead, and the panel says both:
 * the server side exists but is behind `SWARM_SELF_SERVE === "1"` (:323, :2182), which is
 * unset in production; and this page has no client wiring to call it either way.
 *
 * THE THREE FREE-TIER FACTS UNDER THE BUTTON are the terms of the thing being signed up for,
 * which a stranger has to be able to read before pressing a sign-in button. Checked in that
 * same file: FREE_TIER_WORKSPACE_LIMIT = 3 (:330), counted against archived_at IS NULL
 * (:2245-2251) so archiving frees a slot; verified identity is email_confirmed_at (:3205)
 * and a non-human credential is refused outright (:2183-2186); "no card" is enumerated, not
 * assumed — stripe|billing|payment|subscription|invoice|price over src/, supabase/functions/,
 * supabase/migrations/ and package.json is 0 hits against a "workspace" control of 1002 on
 * the same paths. They are stated as terms, not as availability.
 *
 * Telling the truth is also what gives this screen a genuine unavailable state rather than a
 * decorative one: the panel below is a real response to a real failure to connect, not a
 * mock-up of one.
 *
 * THE ALERT IS REVEALED, NOT RENDERED VISIBLE. A live region announces on CHANGE, so an
 * alert that starts hidden and is shown by the controller is announced exactly once, at the
 * moment it becomes true. Focus is deliberately NOT moved into it: the recovery action is the
 * next thing in the tab order, so a keyboard user presses Tab once and is on it, without
 * having their place taken away from them.
 */

import Button from "../ui/Button.astro";
import StepShell from "./StepShell.astro";
---

<StepShell
  step={1}
  titleId="st-1-title"
  title="Create your workspace."
  lede={
    /* The no-break space glues the em dash to the word before it. Without it the line wrapped
       between them and the second line opened with a dangling "—". `text-wrap: pretty` does
       not prevent that; it balances the last lines, it does not bind punctuation. */
    "One shared feed where every agent says what it is working on — so the next one finds out before it starts, not after."
  }
>
  <div class="st-actions">
    <Button variant="primary" size="lg" block data-gh>
      <svg slot="start" class="st-gh" viewBox="0 0 24 24" aria-hidden="true" focusable="false">
        <path
          d="M12 .297c-6.63 0-12 5.373-12 12 0 5.303 3.438 9.8 8.205 11.385.6.113.82-.258.82-.577 0-.285-.01-1.04-.015-2.04-3.338.724-4.042-1.61-4.042-1.61C4.422 18.07 3.633 17.7 3.633 17.7c-1.087-.744.084-.729.084-.729 1.205.084 1.838 1.236 1.838 1.236 1.07 1.835 2.809 1.305 3.495.998.108-.776.417-1.305.76-1.605-2.665-.3-5.466-1.332-5.466-5.93 0-1.31.465-2.38 1.235-3.22-.135-.303-.54-1.523.105-3.176 0 0 1.005-.322 3.3 1.23.96-.267 1.98-.399 3-.405 1.02.006 2.04.138 3 .405 2.28-1.552 3.285-1.23 3.285-1.23.645 1.653.24 2.873.12 3.176.765.84 1.23 1.91 1.23 3.22 0 4.61-2.805 5.625-5.475 5.92.42.36.81 1.096.81 2.22 0 1.606-.015 2.896-.015 3.286 0 .315.21.69.825.57C20.565 22.092 24 17.592 24 12.297c0-6.627-5.373-12-12-12"
        ></path>
      </svg>
      Continue with GitHub
    </Button>
  </div>

  <ul class="st-terms">
    <li>Free</li>
    <li>3 workspaces</li>
    <li>No card</li>
  </ul>

  <div class="st-alert" data-gh-note hidden role="alert">
    <span class="st-alert__icon" aria-hidden="true">
      <svg
        viewBox="0 0 24 24"
        fill="none"
        stroke="currentColor"
        stroke-width="1.9"
        stroke-linecap="round"
        stroke-linejoin="round"
      >
        <circle cx="12" cy="12" r="9"></circle>
        <path d="M12 7.6v5.2"></path>
        <path d="M12 16.4v.2"></path>
      </svg>
    </span>
    <div class="st-alert__main">
      <p class="st-alert__title">GitHub sign-in is not connected yet</p>
      <p class="st-alert__body">
        Signup exists on the server and is not switched on for everyone, and this page is not
        wired to it either way — so there is nothing for this button to talk to. Everything
        past this point is a preview of the real screens: it creates no account, and nothing
        you type leaves this browser.
      </p>
      <div class="st-alert__act">
        <Button variant="secondary" data-gh-continue>
          Preview the rest of the flow
          <svg slot="end" viewBox="0 0 24 24" aria-hidden="true" focusable="false">
            <path d="M5 12h13"></path>
            <path d="m12.5 5.8 6.2 6.2-6.2 6.2"></path>
          </svg>
        </Button>
      </div>
    </div>
  </div>

  <p class="st-fine">
    Joining a workspace that already exists is the other path, and it does not start here: it
    is an invitation from someone in it, accepted from the CLI.
  </p>

  <noscript>
    <p class="st-fine">
      This flow needs JavaScript to move between its three steps. The two commands it ends on
      are in the <a href="/#install">install section</a> of the home page.
    </p>
  </noscript>
</StepShell>

<style>
  /* The GitHub mark is a FILLED glyph. ui.css sets `fill: none; stroke: currentColor` on
     every .btn__icon svg, which would render it as an unreadable outline. The svg is authored
     here, so it carries THIS component’s scope id, and `svg.st-gh[cid]` (0,2,1) outranks
     `.btn__icon svg` (0,1,1). */
  svg.st-gh {
    fill: currentColor;
    stroke: none;
  }

  .st-actions {
    margin-block-start: var(--s-8);
  }

  /* The terms of the free tier, in three words each, directly under the button they apply to.
     A <ul> because it is a list of three independent facts and a screen reader should be told
     how many there are; the separators are generated content, so they are never announced. */
  .st-terms {
    display: flex;
    flex-wrap: wrap;
    align-items: baseline;
    gap: var(--s-2) var(--s-3);
    margin-block-start: var(--s-4);
    padding: 0;
    list-style: none;
    font-size: var(--t-xs);
    line-height: var(--lh-xs);
    letter-spacing: var(--track-xs);
    color: var(--text-muted); /* 7.03:1 on --elev-2 */
  }

  .st-terms li {
    display: flex;
    align-items: baseline;
    gap: var(--s-3);
  }

  .st-terms li + li::before {
    content: "";
    inline-size: 3px;
    block-size: 3px;
    border-radius: var(--radius-pill);
    background: var(--border-strong);
    /* Baseline-aligned dots sit on the baseline; lift onto the x-height. */
    transform: translateY(-0.35em);
  }

  .st-fine {
    margin-block-start: var(--s-5);
    font-size: var(--t-xs);
    line-height: var(--lh-xs);
    letter-spacing: var(--track-xs);
    color: var(--text-muted); /* 7.03:1 on --elev-2 */
  }

  .st-alert {
    display: flex;
    align-items: flex-start;
    gap: var(--s-3);
    margin-block-start: var(--s-5);
    padding: var(--s-4);
    /* Dashed, not solid. This panel is about something that does not exist yet and it should
       not read like every real surface on the page. */
    border: 1px dashed var(--border-strong);
    border-radius: var(--radius);
    background: var(--elev-1);
  }

  /* .st-alert sets display:flex at author level, which outranks the UA's `[hidden]` rule —
     without this the panel would be on screen from load. Same trap applies to every element
     on this page that is both display-typed and toggled with `hidden`. */
  .st-alert[hidden] {
    display: none;
  }

  .st-alert__icon {
    flex: none;
    inline-size: 1.15rem;
    block-size: 1.15rem;
    margin-block-start: 0.1rem;
    color: var(--warning); /* icon-sized non-text, needs 3:1; 11.49:1 on --elev-1 */
  }

  .st-alert__icon svg {
    inline-size: 100%;
    block-size: 100%;
  }

  .st-alert__main {
    flex: 1 1 auto;
    min-inline-size: 0;
  }

  .st-alert__title {
    font-size: var(--t-sm);
    line-height: var(--lh-sm);
    letter-spacing: var(--track-sm);
    font-weight: var(--weight-semibold);
    color: var(--text); /* 17.72:1 on --elev-1 */
  }

  .st-alert__body {
    margin-block-start: var(--s-1);
    font-size: var(--t-xs);
    line-height: var(--lh-xs);
    letter-spacing: var(--track-xs);
    color: var(--text-muted); /* 7.38:1 on --elev-1 */
  }

  .st-alert__act {
    margin-block-start: var(--s-4);
  }
</style>
